      "side": 1,
      "message": "My answer to this is yes, though there is a question of whether to maintain the `ScratchBuffer` wrapper that exists today, which supports sub-allocations and automatically returns a buffer back to the pool when it goes out of scope. I generally like the RAII in that approach while also supporting an explicit return.  \n\nI\u0027ve been meaning to generalize the current `DrawBufferManager::getScratchBuffer`, which is limited to private storage buffers, to uniform and vertex buffers that are transfer copy destinations (which we chatted about today). I can explore moving that logic over here as it\u0027s not particularly tied to DrawBufferManager, although there will be some common logic around managing alignments for the specific usage.\n\nI can picture a scenario in which DrawBufferManager calls out to ScratchResourceManager when it needs a copy destination for transfer buffers.",
      "revId": "8ca58cbbf9a8a59e0fb3037c036d48d9fb451940",
